    "introduction": "Standard Life, formerly Phoenix Group, provides long-term savings and retirement products, including workplace pensions, individual savings and annuities. Its activities combine managing existing policy books with attracting new retirement and pension business. Customers use its products to accumulate savings or convert them into future income, while the group manages assets and obligations over extended periods. Earnings depend on policy charges, insurance economics and the management of capital and investments. The business requires careful matching of assets to future commitments and efficient administration of large policy populations. Customer retention, pension demand, interest rates and longevity assumptions influence outcomes across its different products.",
